      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling. The 1,600 mg single dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nThese are options within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum, and it's usually reserved for inflammatory conditions.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day) for mild to moderate pain.\n\nIf 1600 mg was meant to be the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily, I can enter that. Tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it. If you need more than the labeled maximum, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending first."
      }
     ],
